900 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1822 0 R
/E (Essential Specialization: The Base model failed significantly in Nodule tasks \(~0.04 - 0.06 accuracy\). Fine-tuning was mandatory to achieve diagnostic capability.)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
901 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1823 0 R
/E (The CoT Breakthrough: Chain-of-Thought \(With Explain\) achieved Perfect Accuracy \(1.0\) across multiple Chest Abnormalities \(54, 55, 57\).)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
902 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1824 0 R
/E (Reasoning Recovery: Notably in Chest abn 55, the direct fine-tuned model dropped to 0.21, but CoT recovered it to 1.0, proving that explicit reasoning prevents logical collapses.)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
903 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1825 0 R
/E (Pattern vs. Logic: No-Explain performed better on visual-spatial tasks \(Nodules\), while CoT excelled in complex diagnostic logic.)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
904 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 398 0 R
/E (The Power of Fine-Tuning)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
905 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1826 0 R
/E (Fine-Tuning > Base Model: Across all domains \(Oncology, Cardiology, Radiology\), fine-tuning transformed a non-functional base model into a specialized medical expert.)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
906 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1827 0 R
/E (Clinical Viability: While Base models struggle with zero-shot medical reasoning, LoRA fine-tuning provides the domain-specific knowledge necessary for real-world clinical use.)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
907 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1828 0 R
